“Your deployment pipeline is successful, but the new application version is not reflecting in production. What would you check?”

My approach would be:

1. Verify whether the deployment actually reached the target environment.
2. Check the deployment logs and the application version running on the server/container.
3. If using Kubernetes, check the rollout status, pods, ReplicaSets and image version.
4. Verify whether the deployment is pulling the latest image or using an older cached image.
5. Check the service/ingress routing to make sure traffic is reaching the expected pods.
6. Finally, check application logs and monitoring metrics for any runtime issue.

A successful pipeline doesn't always mean a successful release.

The important part is understanding where the deployment flow stopped — build, image, deployment, routing, or application runtime.
